 "lines": [],
 "notes": "The torpedo boat TA35, ex Giuseppe Dezza (73 x 7.3 m), broken in two by a mine in 1944: the larger stern section upright and the bow section on its port side, about 70 m apart on a flat silty bottom at 34 m (published gaps range from 50 to 100 m). Position 44 58.599 N 13 40.732 E from reiseinfo-kroatien.com, in the Fazana channel between Rovinj and Brijuni, drawn at the stern section; features from Diving Center Shark (buoy on the aft gun, flak, depth-charge gear, fallen torpedo tube, boiler at the break), Caretta Diving and dive3d.eu (two 10.2 cm guns and two quadruple 20 mm mounts, one of which has toppled; which one is not published). No heading is published: both halves are drawn on one NNW axis and the positions along the hull are approximate.",
